  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197500: PostgreSQL crash and half-open recovery

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Pool recovery is qualified against both abrupt database termination and a TCP
connection which remains open but stops delivering server bytes. Query and the
two reset operations retain the host read timeout independently; their bounded
composite is at most three read-timeout intervals. A timed-out or reset-failed
physical connection is evicted. Recovery grows a fresh TLS/SCRAM connection
without exposing reconnect or socket authority to the guest.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 is stopped using `pg_ctl -m immediate`, then restarted
through crash recovery; the unchanged pool token establishes a new working
connection. A bounded TLS-transparent proxy subsequently stalls only the
server-to-client direction while retaining the TCP connection. Query and reset
fail within the three-operation bound, the connection is evicted, forwarding
resumes and a new lease/query succeeds with no native handle leak.

This closes immediate crash and half-open timeout recovery. Version/platform
matrices, prolonged packet-loss distributions and long-duration contention
soak remain open."}]
